{
  "id": "andon-latticed",
  "description": "Four panes to a face. A bar runs the full height of the opening and a rail crosses it at half height, both lapped into the frame the same way the frame is lapped into itself — so the divisions are one more course of the same joint rather than a grille laid over the paper. The bar takes its housing at the crossing and the rail takes the other half of the wood, which is why the pair reads as solid from the front.",
